  "scope": "Stage4J3: D3D9 volume sampler private storage holds separate from shared parent/cached volume-level public refs, with device pins only on public0->1/1->0. Reusable storage teardown unlinks then clears parent/all mip stores, cached views and slice shadows before releasing the public device pin last. Live SetTexture, replacement, device cleanup and Reset use private volume refs; all2D/cube/volume private sampler slots no longer discount external public Reset blockers. Native actual lifetime/set/query/reset/cleanup methods with constructor/emitter stubs:70656 new checks,1024 pool/order profiles,8192 public-zero revivals,two cached levels and64 mixed2D/cube/volume replacement cycles;14 strict runtime-assertion mutants, old actual volume methods plus new helpers runtime negative control and ASAN/UBSAN. Retains86784 actual2D and104192 cube observations. XP constructs one4x4x4 DEFAULT dynamic volume with2x2x2 mip and six slice uploads,128 parent/level/container revivals with exact device pins and256 private queries. Four base slices sampled,one retained volume-view edits only base slice2 with neighbor3 preserved, explicit mip filtering/max mip selects two smaller mip slices. Parent and child-only public references separately block Reset; binding-only volume permits Reset and post-Reset clear. Seven exact slice uploads, eight draws, one clear and nine actual readbacks have simulated XP transport pixels; independent GPU replay validates576 pixels and exact volume destruction after Reset before further drawing, with empty guest maps before genuine owner release. Recording/stateblock public holds retain prior semantics. D3D8/buffer/shader/stateblock binding refs,general external-child root-state retention,arbitrary callback/concurrency/loss/full Reset/format/MSAA/fullscreen/multi-buffer/wrapper conversion,native HAL,games/FPS and overall stages4/5/6 remain open. Host/protocol/shader/bundle and D3D8/DDraw unchanged.",
